<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<resources>
    <!-- Dark launch theme so the window never flashes white before Compose
         takes over. The real theming is the Material 3 ColorScheme in code.

         The parent MUST stay an AppCompat descendant. MediaRouter's Cast
         chooser is a MediaRouteChooserDialog, which extends AppCompatDialog,
         and it is built from the *Activity's* theme — the Theme.AppCompat
         wrapper CastButton.kt applies to the button widget never reaches it.
         MediaRouterThemeHelper layers R.style.Theme_MediaRouter on top, but
         that is parented to ThemeOverlay.AppCompat.Dark, and a ThemeOverlay
         by design defines only a few colour attrs — not windowActionBar. So
         with a platform (android:Theme.Material) parent, nothing in the
         chain defines it and AppCompatDelegateImpl.createSubDecor() throws
         "You need to use a Theme.AppCompat theme (or descendant) with this
         activity." on the main thread, crashing on every tap of the cast
         icon.

         This was previously "fixed" by hand-copying AppCompat's colorPrimary/
         colorPrimaryDark/colorAccent/isLightTheme onto a Material parent.
         That got past an earlier crash in the same dialog — without
         colorPrimary, MediaRouterThemeHelper.getControllerColor() resolves a
         fully transparent colour and ColorUtils.calculateContrast() throws
         "background can not be translucent: #0" — and then landed on the
         next missing attr. Impersonating AppCompat attr by attr does not
         work; the theme has to be one.

         The four colour items below stay, but now as deliberate overrides of
         AppCompat's defaults: they keep the chooser dialog dark and tinted
         Sky-blue. Values match SkyPalette.Accent/Canvas in Theme.kt. -->
    <style name="Theme.Skyline" parent="Theme.AppCompat.NoActionBar">
        <item name="android:windowBackground">#0A0E1A</item>
        <item name="android:statusBarColor">@android:color/transparent</item>
        <item name="android:navigationBarColor">@android:color/transparent</item>
        <item name="colorPrimary">#0B69F5</item>
        <item name="colorPrimaryDark">#05070A</item>
        <item name="colorAccent">#0B69F5</item>
        <item name="isLightTheme">false</item>
    </style>
</resources>
